      "content": "it's easy to talk about \"tools and funding\" but for a small shop like mine, the upfront cost of new equipment is way higher than some government grant is ever gonna cover. it feels like the \"environmental benefit\" is being used to justify a policy that's basically just picking winners and losers. why can't the EPA just focus on the big polluters instead of making small businesses jump through these hoops? isn't it kind of unfair to put the burden on us when we're such a tiny part of the problem?",
